WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.680
What’s goin on thugz? This week we
can’t stop won’t stop with

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.300
"The Old Man and The Sea" by Ernest Hemingway.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.900
It’s been eighty-four straight days since old fisherman Santiago dun caught his ass a fish.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:29.680
Matter of fact, this geezer so sh** out of luck dat Manolin, his lil thug-in-training, gotta bail on him.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.240
Manny’s folks lay down the law and tell him he gotta crew up with some other hustla

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.820
who makin it rain fish on the reg.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.660
But even though they ain’t ridin’ tight no mo, 
Manolin still got Santiago’s back.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.140
Erry night he helps Santiago truck his
gear back to the crib where they chop game

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.680
bout their main man Joe DiMaggio.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:53.440
And just like Joey D, Santiago
gonna stay on his game til the day he go.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.320
So later, Santiago gets up on his hoopty and
treks out farther than he usually do.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.340
As he chillin in the deep, his line hook a BIG-ASS Marlin.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.640
Look, this fish got such a fat ass that he pulls 
the whole boat with him as he try to jet.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.860
But Santiago ain’t backin down.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.740
No matter how much it hurt to hang on to dat
line, he ain’t lettin go.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.360
A day goes by and both Santiago and
dat fish still goin hard.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.680
Santiago thinkin, “I feel yo pain brutha.”

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.000
After three days of raw doggin his
mits, Santiago shanks da marlin with his harpoon,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.980
straps it to his ride, and starts flowin home.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.799
But soon a shark creeps up on da
boat and and starts grubbin on dat marlin.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.220
Santiago all like “hell nah. Best step off
my fish, son!”

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:45.060
So he chunks his harpoon right through dat shark’s dome, but loses his piece in da process. Damn.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.720
When mo’ sharks start lurkin round
the boat, Santiago wonderss if all this pain

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:55.360
mighta been for nothin. But our boy don’t
quit. He gonna ghetto rig himself a shiv and

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:00.780
keep stabbin dem haters. Even though Santiago
keepin it real as he can, them fat-ass sharks

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.810
ain’t done til dat marlin ain’t nothin but bones.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:08.479
After Santiago gets back to the
shore, all the hoods on the block gather round

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.680
to peep game at the gnarly fish skeleton.
It’s so damn big they be thinkin ol Santiago

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.300
caught himself a shark.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.580
Then Manolin drops in on Santiago’s
crib while he catchin some Z’s.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:25.760
When he peeps how jacked up the dat geezer’s hands
be from warrin with da fish, fool busts in to tears.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.380
Santiago’s crusty ass wakes up, chops game with Manny, and they decide

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:36.300
to become fishing partners again. Then Santiago crashes and dreams his usual dream:

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.740
lions chillin on the beach.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.400
Ain’t no doubt bout this book’s
main theme:

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:50.440
Man can beast through even the nastiest 
pain when he got his eye on the prize.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:55.580
And for old man Santiago, the prize
ain’t just flippin dat Marlin for some phat coin,

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:00.340
but to show out and prove dat even though
his old ass might be sh**ting in diapers,

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.300
he still got the juice.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:08.540
In all Hemingway’s books, there are two kinds of bruthas: the big dawgs and the lil ol bitches.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.720
The bitches are nothin but yo ordinary 
scrubs who who cool with just bein normal,

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.019
but the Big-Dawgs be all the G-ed up heros

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:22.739
who break off all society’s haters and chase a life outside of what’s normal, like my man Santiago.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:28.840
Fool takes it to the next level when he literally 
goes out farther to fish than errybody else.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.080
Not only dat, but Santiago throws up his middle
finger to society’s

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.540
superficial bullsh**, keeps it trill, and
gets tight wit mama nature.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.580
All up in this text we seein Santiago 
tied to nature’s little homies:

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.280
And if you think it stops there,
you straight trippin.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.900
On the real, the main animal Santiago 
associated with is dat marlin.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.400
Some scholas even think dat fish
reppin Jesus.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:28.360
See, to some Christians, dis world only meaningful
because of Jesus’s pain and sacrifice.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.680
And for Santiago, it ain't no different:

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:36.200
Homie's life is meaningful because of that fish beastin through pain and sacrificing his life.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:40.800
And since Santiago feelin
da hurt too, he also representin da big JC.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.700
But just cuz you roughin through the sh** don’t 
mean you always gonna come out on top.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:55.180
Life ain’t about that, blood.
It’s bout strugglin to live til yo last breath.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:59.720
As Santiago say: 
“A man can be destroyed, but not defeated.”

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:03.849
So fight the good fight by hittin
dat subscribe button and tellin yo friends.

00:05:03.849 --> 00:05:05.829
Catch you next week. Peace!

